# Allow-list: this repo only tracks code, the README, and this file.
# Everything else — images, datasets, the virtual env, model weights, training
# run artifacts/logs, generated output files (gp5/xml/musicxml/debug pngs),
# caches, and OS/editor cruft — is excluded, whatever it's named or where it
# lives, rather than trying to list every kind of "general thing" by hand.

# Ignore everything by default...
*

# ...but still look inside every directory (otherwise git won't even check
# whether something further down matches one of the re-include rules below)
!*/

# ...and re-include exactly what should be tracked, at any depth.
!.gitignore
!README
!*.py

# README screenshots — explicit exceptions since the README embeds these.
!noteOutput.png
!rhythmOutput.png
!output-1.png

# Re-exclude vendored/virtual-env trees even though they're full of .py files
# that would otherwise match the rule above — these aren't "your" code.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
datasets
images
runs

# NOTE: this is an allow-list, not a blocklist — anything new you want tracked
# (requirements.txt, a LICENSE, docs/, etc.) needs its own "!pattern" line
# added below, or it'll be silently excluded like everything else.
